#
# procd reads this file once ubusd runs. The format is
# <id>:<runlevels>:<action>:<process>: the id names the terminal (empty: none,
# the program reads and writes /dev/null), the runlevels are ignored. procd
# reads up to 127 characters of a line and the first 7 words of a command: a
# longer one is cut short.
#
# The stick's programs are procd's services, which the boot script starts in
# their order (onu-svc): procd starts each again when it ends, and tells how
# often it did (onu-svc list). Only the console's login is a program of this
# file, started again half a second after it ends.

# The boot script, /etc/init.d/rcS, as /etc/rc.d/S10boot: procd runs the
# scripts of /etc/rc.d whose names begin with S, in order, with "boot".
::sysinit:/etc/init.d/rcS S boot

# At a restart or a halt, the scripts of /etc/rc.d whose names begin with K,
# with "shutdown": the image has none. procd goes on to end every program and
# restart only once this is done, so without the line it would wait for ever,
# feeding the watchdog.
::shutdown:/etc/init.d/rcS K shutdown

# A login prompt on the console, started again whenever the session ends. The
# one account is root, with the password that ssh and the panel take too
# (onu-config keeps it; until one is set it is "admin"). A bench may have root's
# shell there without the password (onu-run, CONSOLE_AUTOLOGIN in
# /etc/board.conf). The speed stays the one the boot loader set, 115200 baud.
console::respawnlate:/usr/lib/onu/onu-run console
